option.DISTANT_HORIZONS_SHADOWMAP = §c(DO NOT USE IF YOU DO NOT KNOW WHAT THIS IS)§r DH shadowmap support
option.DISTANT_HORIZONS_SHADOWMAP.comment =  §cTHIS SETTING WILL DESTROY PERFORMANCE THIS WILL MAKE SHADOWS LOOK BLOCKY, FLICKERY, AND LOW DETAIL§r. set shadow distance to 32 chunks (or more). set shadow resolution to 4096 (or more)
option.TOGGLE_VL_FOG = Toggle Volumetric Fog
option.TOGGLE_VL_FOG.comment = one big button to just turn all the fog off.

option.TRANSLUCENT_COLORED_SHADOWS.comment = §bWhat is this?§r This effect allows translucent things like stained glass to color the sunlight as it passes through it. §aPERFORMANCE COST:§r medium
option.MINIMUM_WATER_ABSORBANCE.comment = §bWhat is this?§r This controls how "clear" the water is in shallow areas. AUTO allows water to be clear outdoors, but adjust to be at a minimum value of 7 when indoors, to make it clearly visible. §dTHIS SETTING DOES NOT IMPACT UNDER-WATER VISUALS.        

option.SATURATION.comment = §bWhat is this?§r This controls how "colorful" the image is. negative values take away colors - positive values make them more intense.
option.CROSSTALK.comment = §bWhat is this?§r This is a modifier of saturation - it offsets the saturation of the BRIGHT parts of the image.
option.WHITE_BALANCE.comment = §bWhat is this?§r This controls how warm or cool the image looks - it balances the blues and reds.
option.TAA_MODE.comment = §bStandard:§r has the best antialiasing ability - uses more jitter offsets, but needs more frame history (set blend factor lower), it will flicker more and have more motion artifacts. §bResponsive:§r has the worst antialiasing ability - uses fewer jitter offsets, needs less frame history (set blend factor higher), so it can have fewer motion artifacts. §bTemporal Upscaling:§r Render the shader at a lower window resolution, and then scale it back up to fit the screen for better performance - has MANY artifacts.
option.MOTION_BLUR.comment = §bWhat is this?§r This effect makes the entire screen blur in whatever direction you move the camera, or wherever you move within the world. §aPERFORMANCE COST:§r very low
option.CHROMATIC_ABERRATION.comment = §bWhat is this?§r This effect makes the edges of the screen have a color shift of red and blue. §aPERFORMANCE COST:§r very very low
option.VIGNETTE.comment = §bWhat is this?§r This effect makes the edges of the screen increasingly dark the closer to the edges it gets. §aPERFORMANCE COST:§r very very low
option.TONEMAP.comment = §bWhat is this?§r This fits the internal HDR or whatever range of color the shader is doing, to look nice on your SDR monitor. it will control general color processing - the contrast, saturation, white point, black point, hue shift, path to white, ect - each one has a different look

option.DOF_QUALITY.comment= §bWhat is this?§r This is the "un-focus" blur in the background and foreground when a camera focuses its lense on something, sometimes referred to as "bokeh". §aPERFORMANCE COST:§r low to high
option.MANUAL_FOCUS.comment= §bWhat is this?§r control how the camera lense focuses. "Auto-Focus" will focus on what you look at. "brightness Slider" lets you manually focus using the brightness setting in video settings. "Manual Focus" only focuses on a fixed point some distance away from the camera in meters.
option.DOF_ANAMORPHIC_RATIO.comment= §bWhat is this?§r This is a recreation of the Anamorphic lense distorion, where it will stretch the out of focus/bokeh. 
